+# 0.31 to 0.32 migration
+
+Public version remains Cyberforteca 0.3. This is internal revision 0.32, not
+production security. The baseline is the original `cyberforteca` 0.31 package,
+identified by TrustedSnapshot, ownership_binding_ref and decisions.jsonl.
+The separate `cf031_terra` variant is not modified by this iteration.
+
+The original architecture and all 32 boundary test intentions are retained.
+Changes are concentrated in the existing models, evaluator, interfaces,
+serialization and fixtures. SMC is a small additional model/simulation module.
+The 0.2 source-review document is preserved unchanged as historical context.
+
+## Breaking API and schema changes
+
+| 0.31 | 0.32 migration |
+| --- | --- |
+| Positional multi-field record construction | Use field keywords for every multi-field model, PolicyRule, Policy and TrustedSnapshot. Single-value Ref/Label/Digest wrappers remain positional. |
+| Bare local_identity/peer_identity enum | Supply separate IdentityResult objects or None. Verifier output must bind subject, root, enrollment, session, challenge, clock, result reference, verification time and expiry. Never wrap an old VERIFIED flag as proof. |
+| Session with only attestation refs | Supply local_identity_ref, peer_identity_ref and handshake_started_at, plus typed attestation refs. |
+| Arbitrary differing requested/effective scope | Only the reviewed EXPORT_OWNED_DATA -> READ_OWNED_DATA relation on the same resource is accepted, and it still needs an explicit rule. |
+| PolicyRule grants DELETE_AUDIT_HISTORY | Remove such rules. Requests remain representable and always deny. Detail-cache purge is a separate owner capability, not a renamed audit deletion. |
+| Grant without key binding | Re-evaluate and issue new grants. Never upgrade cached 0.31 grants by inserting the current epoch. 0.32 binds key_epoch and key_handle_ref and provides validate_grant. |
+| SessionContext.granted_scope | Removed. Resolve authority only from the protected grant registry. No scope projection on a session is authoritative. |
+| RecoveryPrincipal.owner_ref | Use OwnerPrincipal with nominal OwnerId and an independent registry reference. |
+| RecoveryVerifier -> RecoveryContext | Return RecoveryVerificationResult only. Core constructs RecoveryContext separately from a verifier result and registry binding. |
+| RecoveryContext.allowed_scope | Removed. Policy.recovery_ceiling and the selected recovery-specific rule determine the effective scope. |
+| Unchecked ownership_binding_ref | Resolve and enforce a matching OwnershipBinding for the verified owner, exact resource, policy, status, clock and validity interval. Missing/mismatched bindings deny. |
+| Implicit ownership context for owned operations | Supply request.owner_id and either OwnerVerificationResult or an independently verified recovery principal, plus the matching ownership registry binding. |
+| Broad RESTORE_OWNERSHIP_ACCESS | Scope requires restoration=OwnershipAccess.OWNED_DATA_READ. This restores only that owner's read-only resource view within the grant lifetime. No roles, credentials, registry bindings or secondary grants are created. |
+| Outcome identified only by decision/request/grant | AuthorityOutcome.snapshot_digest binds the exact evaluated model snapshot, including verification provenance. Audit projection re-evaluates and compares it. It is not a signature or trust proof. |
+| Audit peer_device meant requester's destination | peer_device now means session.peer_device_id from the core's perspective. New local_device identifies the evaluating/resource side. |
+| Generic audit identity/attestation/verifier fields | Rename to explicit local_identity_*, peer_identity_*, local_attestation_* and peer_attestation_*. Add recovery_result_ref and key_epoch. |
+| CF031 serialization | CF032 envelope, changed fields and snapshots. Preserve old audit bytes as CF031. Do not reinterpret or rewrite historical records as CF032. |
+
+## Handshake and transitions
+
+Results may predate establishment, but not handshake_started_at. The candidate
+SessionId and fresh challenges must exist before evidence acquisition.
+At decision time, both result intervals and the established session must be
+valid. Bounds are inclusive at start and exclusive at expiry. Tests include
+handshake start 20, establishment 100, attestation expiry 800, acceptance at
+799 and denial at 800, with both sides independently tested.
+
+Existing grants never migrate on session or key changes. validate_grant checks
+current epoch AND key handle, lifetime, current policy, principals, channel,
+appraisals, liveness and ownership. It does not refresh or mutate the grant.
+Production must resolve grants from protected state and make validation/use
+atomic. Persistent epoch monotonicity and rollback protection are not implemented.
+
+## Changed or strengthened invariants
+
+1. RESTRICTED is an explicitly allowlisted strict reduction, not arbitrary substitution.
+2. Permanent audit deletion cannot be represented as an ordinary grant.
+3. Identity proof is fresh, subject/root/enrollment/session/challenge-bound on both sides.
+4. Both identity and attestation are no earlier than the handshake boundary.
+5. Session authority has one source, grants, and is bound to the current key epoch/handle.
+6. Recovery verification proves identity/evidence only. Policy determines authority.
+7. Ownership authority requires the verified owner and an enforced registry binding.
+8. Restoration is a one-owner, one-resource read-only view, never role restoration or delegation.
+9. Decision audit binds the exact evaluated snapshot and uses consistent local/peer attribution.
+10. Permanent skeletons survive optional detail-cache purge. Success produces a correlated receipt.
+11. Multi-field records require keywords. Internal IDs retain nominal types.
+12. Decoding must use the versioned field schema, never guesses from string contents.
+
+Preserved: capability != authority, authentication != authorization,
+evidence != verified result, verified identity != authority,
+attestation result != authority, recovery verification != recovery authority,
+device identity != application identity, session identity != channel/counter,
+unknown != malicious, and loss of liveness != compromise.
+
+## SMC integration contract
+
+CFDecisionRecord remains the canonical structured decision explanation.
+DecisionSkeleton is its permanent, non-secret allowlist projection. Optional
+DetailCacheEntry records belong to an owner/resource and contain only references
+to protected details. Do not put credentials or sensitive payloads in either model.
+
+PURGE_OWNED_DETAIL_CACHE needs exact owner authority, current verification and
+ownership binding, an explicit rule, and a recovery ceiling if using recovery.
+purge_detail_cache models an atomic-by-value transition that preserves permanent
+skeletons and appends PurgeReceipt. Its execution point is explicitly
+SIMULATION.SMC.CACHE. It does not erase files or implement durable storage.
+Production must commit a successful receipt atomically with actual purge.
+
+Opaque audit IDs can still be privacy-relevant. Access/retention policy remains
+necessary even though no credential contents or optional details enter the ledger.
+
+## Confirmed-defect evidence
+
+`tests/test_regressions.py` runs unchanged against either original 0.31 or 0.32.
+All twelve probes fail against 0.31 by assertion, without import/runtime errors.
+They pass after the fixes. Some probes detect missing architectural contracts
+rather than demonstrate an exploitable production system, which never existed.
+See TEST_MATRIX.md and TEST_RESULTS.txt for exact coverage and executed results.
+
+The four mutation runs each delete the entire local or peer entry from one
+identity/attestation checking loop. Each is caught by assertions with all other
+prerequisites valid. This is targeted mutation evidence, not exhaustive mutation
+coverage, formal verification or a claim of production security.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- Verification, app measurement provenance, trusted registries and isolation are synthetic inputs.
+- Python construction and frozen records are not authentication or an attacker boundary.
+- No production identity/TPM, AEAD, key store, transport, replay acceptance or handshake exists.
+- No RecoveryKey/biometric verifier, actual credential recovery or data decryption recovery exists.
+- No real ownership restoration or general resource enforcement exists.
+- No persistent SMC ledger/cache, secure deletion, crash recovery or protected chain anchor exists.
+- No untrusted decoder exists. CF032 canonical JSON is a local test/audit encoding, not a final wire standard.
+- No automatic grant migration or reissuance exists. No durable epoch rollback protection exists.
+- Policy references and issuer/result IDs are supplied by the trusted fixture. Production must authenticate them and bind policy digests to actual policy content.
+- No full 0.2 repository integration, MOSKO OS build, formal proof or independent production security audit was performed.
+- Neural stimulation, biological writes, full REA/HMAI and autonomous policy modification remain out of scope.
